description:
FILED s543m (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-27), from the measurement of the review's F1 row 16 (which decides: the modifier or the capture?  The MODIFIER: a plain lexical with a modifier was not flushed either, for EVERY drop shape -- `Pl::Stmt::expr_shape` returned before the drop shapes when a modifier was present, and `_lower_expr_stmt`'s `$drop_ok` refused `$mod`).  s543m (WIP 11) took the modifier where it is the same place: every drop shape of `_lower_expr_stmt` (an element store of undef, a void delete / pop / shift / splice) under `if` / `unless` is flushed now.  What is LEFT is this task.  PRE-EXISTING: base 9a3ce86f the same.

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 | ./runpcl; scratch/s543m/p11/rows.pl prog 7):
    my $f = "/tmp/x.$$"; sub mk { open my $t, ">", $f or die; print $t "hdata"; $t } sub sz { my $s = -s $f; unlink $f; $s // "none" }
    my $fh = mk(); undef $fh if 1; print "a ", sz(), "\n";
    my %h = (fh => mk()); %h = () if 1; print "b ", sz(), "\n";
    my $x = mk(); $x = undef unless 0; print "c ", sz(), "\n";
    my %t; sub dt { delete $t{fh} if 1 } $t{fh} = mk(); dt(); print "d ", sz(), "\n";
    sub zap { $_[0] = undef } my $hv = mk(); zap($hv); print "e ", sz(), "\n";
perl: a 5 / b 5 / c 5 / d 5 / e 5.  PCL (base and tree at 6dfbf2db): a 0 / b 0 / c 0 / d 0 / e 0.

WHERE: a b c -- the block-level path (`Parser2::_lower_block_1` -> `_fh_drop_flush_var` / `_fh_drop_name`: `_fh_drop_stmt_sym` matches the statement's tokens with no modifier, and the flush is emitted as a separate form BEFORE the statement, so a modifier needs the flush inside the condition: `(p-if C (progn (p-flush-dropped-handle $fh) STMT))`); d -- a TAIL with a modifier takes `_lower_expr_stmt`'s early ret-var return (`_modifier_ret_form`) before the drop wrap; e -- `@_` is in the partition's exception set, which `Parser2::_drop_holder_cl_p` refuses for the element store (right for `@_ = ()`, which drops only the aliases; a store THROUGH `$_[0]` drops the caller's value).


=== APPENDED s543m (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-27): the reviewing session's rm3 w-01 row 7 is THIS task ===
`our %g = (fh => $fh); ... %g = () unless c(0);` is not flushed (perl flushes), while `pop @a unless 0;`, `delete $h{fh} if 1;` and `$g{fh} = undef if c(1);` are (w-01, 15 of 16 rows = perl on 5d426786).  Which of the three decides -- measured in one step (scratch/s543m/p11/w7.pl, `PCL_OPT=-line-track ./pl2cl`): the CLEAR SHAPE under a modifier, whatever the modifier, the condition or the holder.  `%g = () unless c(0);`, `%g = () if 1;`, `%h = () if 1;` (a plain lexical), `undef %h if 1;` and `$x = undef if 1;` all lower to a bare `(p-if C (p-hash-= ...))` / `(p-if C (p-undef %h))` / `(p-if C (p-my-= $x (p-undef)))` with no flush; `$g{fh} = undef unless c(0);` and `pop @a unless c(0);` take the wrap inside the `p-if` (s543m's WIP 11).  So the `unless` and the call condition are fine; the variable shapes (`undef $x;` `$x = undef;` `%h = ();` `@a = ();` `undef %h;` `undef @a;`) are matched by `Parser2::_fh_drop_stmt_sym` on the statement's whole token list (a modifier makes it no match) and their flush is a SEPARATE form emitted before the statement at block level -- not the wrap s543m widened, so not taken (the review: only a one-token miss in the same wrap).
